WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.089 --> 00:00:02.699
Film Courage: What do you think makes a boring
character to you?

00:00:02.699 --> 00:00:09.870
West Liang: I think a character with no inner
life.

00:00:09.870 --> 00:00:21.410
I think for me if some character has some
inner life (if that makes sense).

00:00:21.410 --> 00:00:28.789
Whether that inner life is subtext or whether
that inner life is in conflict with his public

00:00:28.789 --> 00:00:31.140
life or her public life.

00:00:31.140 --> 00:00:37.100
That’s interesting to me.

00:00:37.100 --> 00:00:45.640
I think it really depends on the kind of story
that it is.

00:00:45.640 --> 00:00:47.730
To make the comparison of making a meal.

00:00:47.730 --> 00:00:58.059
I think every meal is different and it commands
a different kind of ingredient.

00:00:58.059 --> 00:01:06.520
I certainly don’t feel like I have all the
answers by any means.

00:01:06.520 --> 00:01:09.640
For me, I’m still trying to figure things
out on my own.

00:01:09.640 --> 00:01:17.759
And I’m trying to figure things out based
on my own kind of sensibilities, my own way

00:01:17.759 --> 00:01:21.359
of writing.

00:01:21.359 --> 00:01:33.420
I think having some kind of life…what about
you?

00:01:33.420 --> 00:01:38.149
Film Courage: I’m even thinking of a movie
that was light and fluffy like LEGALLY BLOND.

00:01:38.149 --> 00:01:41.109
It was still interesting (her character).

00:01:41.109 --> 00:01:43.039
You want to see her [win].

00:01:43.039 --> 00:01:50.500
She doesn’t get easily taken aback by all
these jabs that are thrown her way.

00:01:50.500 --> 00:01:52.840
And you’re like “Wow, that’s kind of
interesting?”

00:01:52.840 --> 00:01:56.549
She keeps being light, bubbly and happy when
most people would be giving them [her detractors]

00:01:56.549 --> 00:01:59.020
the middle finger after awhile, you know?

00:01:59.020 --> 00:02:00.020
[Laughs].

00:02:00.020 --> 00:02:01.020
And so [as the viewer] you’re like “Wow?

00:02:01.020 --> 00:02:02.020
I find her interesting.”

00:02:02.020 --> 00:02:06.459
That’s kind of a light and fun film but
there is still a message behind it.

00:02:06.459 --> 00:02:08.670
It’s a studio film that wasn’t boring.

00:02:08.670 --> 00:02:12.370
It was interesting enough to keep my attention
and I’m sure a lot of other people’s,

00:02:12.370 --> 00:02:13.370
as well.

00:02:13.370 --> 00:02:17.340
West Liang: I mean it’s an incredibly crafted
screenplay.

00:02:17.340 --> 00:02:26.930
On a plot level in terms of where things happen
in terms of having this first kind of pre-life

00:02:26.930 --> 00:02:33.720
and how that changes and inciting incidents
and all that stuff.

00:02:33.720 --> 00:02:36.340
But you look at her character [Reese Witherspoon
as Elle] and she’s battling again expectations

00:02:36.340 --> 00:02:47.400
of her, that people have with who she might
be and what her inner life might be.

00:02:47.400 --> 00:02:52.440
There are plot-driven stories and there are
character-driven stories and I think they

00:02:52.440 --> 00:03:00.159
sort of overlap in a lot of areas, but generally
speaking if you’re talking about a character

00:03:00.159 --> 00:03:13.650
for me, if there is something about that character
that tells me that either that person isn’t

00:03:13.650 --> 00:03:18.069
telling everything about his life or her life.

00:03:18.069 --> 00:03:27.129
Or there is something about that person where
what he or she is doing in front of people

00:03:27.129 --> 00:03:30.549
is different from what they’re doing behind-the-scenes,
for me that’s interesting.

